tests/toc-coverage/fixture_transform_ext/
================================================

A minimal, do-nothing C extension whose only purpose is to make a real
`CREATE TRANSFORM` possible when capturing tests/toc-coverage/fixture.sql's
output.

Why this exists: a TRANSFORM's FROM SQL/TO SQL functions must take or
return the pseudo-type `internal`, which only a C-language function may
use (PostgreSQL rejects any other language for them) -- there is no way
to create one with plain SQL/plpgsql alone. The two functions below do
nothing useful; they only exist to satisfy that signature requirement.

Not needed to build or run pgcopydb itself -- only to regenerate
fixture.dump/expected-pg-restore-list.txt from fixture.sql against a real
Postgres server. To do so:

    cd tests/toc-coverage/fixture_transform_ext
    make
    sudo make install        # or: run as the same user as the target
                              # Postgres server's own binaries
    psql -d <fixture database> -c 'create extension fixture_transform;'

then run the `CREATE TRANSFORM` statement from fixture.sql as usual (it's
a plain SQL statement, not part of the extension itself, so the TRANSFORM
it creates is dumped as its own standalone object, not hidden as an
extension member).
